  "notes": "Central Airlines (中州航空, ICAO HLF, IATA I9): FAA JO 7340.2 lists HLF as CENTRAL AIRLINES CO., LTD, China, telephony HOMELAND. Measured on B-227W (left, 2026-06-01): the Chinese runs x 0.120-0.230 and the English 0.237-0.443, both with a cap height about 1.45 m; on B-227H (right, 2026-07-09) the same stretches within 0.01. The fin mosaic's tiles are square on the aircraft (about 1.6 m), each its own shade: drawn as 11 areas, the one white tile is the fin's base. A partner sticker ('CARGO CITY Katowice Airport') under the forward titles on B-227W only, not drawn. The ex-DHL 777Fs B-226W and B-226Y (the ones seen on HLF flights at LAX) wear a yellow variant (liveries/HLF/yellow.json); two 777Fs (B-2079, B-2082) wear a YunExpress special (teal aft fuselage, green pixel band), not drawn. Colours by eye. The 'from' year is left out: no dated source for the scheme's introduction in hand.",
  "history": "New in the LAX round (2026-11-20); Central Airlines had no scheme here before."
